{"id":"b0842e8d40362b1d31decb6c1728b15fff6d3a5f","axis":"silent","repo":"axios/axios","sha":"b0842e8d40362b1d31decb6c1728b15fff6d3a5f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"PRE_RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@"," "," ## Bug Fixes"," ","+- **XHR adapter cookie access:** Read eligible XSRF cookies through the asynchronous Cookie Store API when supported, avoiding synchronous cookie access while preserving existing URI decoding, malformed-value handling, and fallback behavior. Cookie preparation shares the configured request timeout and cancellation lifecycle; late results cannot send canceled or expired requests. Fetch behavior, public options, and token values remain compatible. (**[#11166](https://github.com/axios/axios/pull/11166)**, closes **[#10826](https://github.com/axios/axios/issues/10826)**)"," - **Node HTTP adapter - proxy tunnel TLS options:** Apply `https.globalAgent` TLS options, including a custom `ca`, to HTTPS origins reached through CONNECT proxies when no per-request `httpsAgent` is supplied. Read origin TLS options for each request so cached tunneling agents pick up changes to the selected agent or a replacement global agent. Explicit agents retain precedence, and the HTTPS proxy connection retains its existing TLS configuration. No new API or type changes. (**#11178**, related to **#11176**; the reported explicit-agent failure remains unverified.)"," - **Percent-encoded Base64 data URLs:** Decode URL-escaped Base64 alphabet, padding, and whitespace before converting the Node HTTP adapter's data URL response. Estimate the Buffer backing allocation after the same decoding so encoded alphabet and padding no longer inflate byte-limit checks, while avoiding the per-character decoding scan for unescaped Base64. Ordinary Base64 inputs, forgiving Buffer decoding, and case-insensitive URL schemes and Base64 markers are preserved; pre-allocation limits still count ignored characters and content after padding. (**[#11294](https://github.com/axios/axios/pull/11294)**)"," - **URL scheme casing:** Accept uppercase and mixed-case supported schemes in the XHR adapter and Node data URLs. Keep data URL allocation estimates aligned with decoding so configured limits reject oversized inputs before Buffer allocation, including ignored Base64 tails. URL paths, query values, payload casing, and unsupported-protocol rejection remain unchanged; no new API or type changes. (**[#11163](https://github.com/axios/axios/pull/11163)**)"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"PRE_RELEASE_DOCS.md","lines":["@@ -20,6 +20,16 @@ Do not store raw diffs or line-number-only instructions here; prefer stable sect"," "," ## Unreleased"," ","+### Asynchronous XSRF cookie reads in the XHR adapter","+","+- **Change:** Document the XHR adapter's use of the Cookie Store API for XSRF token reads.","+- **Source:** `PRE_RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md` Bug Fixes, XHR adapter cookie access; PR #11166 and issue #10826.","+- **Status:** Pending.","+- **Docs targets:** README and request-config guidance for `xsrfCookieName`, `xsrfHeaderName`, and `withXSRFToken`; browser support notes; translated docs after the English documentation is finalized.","+- **Required content:** Explain that the XHR adapter automatically uses `window.cookieStore` when available to avoid synchronous `document.cookie` access while resolving an eligible XSRF token. Browsers without Cookie Store support retain the existing `document.cookie` behavior, and a failed Cookie Store read also falls back to that path. Both read paths preserve Axios's existing URI decoding (once), with malformed escape sequences left unchanged. Cookie lookup and the subsequent XHR share the configured timeout; both cancellation APIs also work during lookup, and late results cannot dispatch a canceled or expired request. The Fetch adapter and the public request-config surface are unchanged; no migration is required.","+- **Examples:** None required because capability detection is automatic and adds no configuration.","+- **Notes:** Keep the explanation scoped to XHR XSRF reads; do not imply that all cookie operations or the Fetch adapter use Cookie Store. Issue #10826 originally requested raw values; compatibility requires retaining Axios's existing decoding because Cookie Store does not percent-decode stored cookies.","+"," ### Opt-in UTF-8 Basic auth usernames"," "," - **Change:** Added `transitional.encodeBasicAuthUsername`, a boolean defaulting to `false`, to opt into UTF-8 encoding of `auth.username` during XHR/Fetch config resolution."],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/adapters/xhr.js","lines":["@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ import normalizeURLForProtocolCheck from '../helpers/normalizeURLForProtocolChec"," import parseProtocol from '../helpers/parseProtocol.js';"," import platform from '../platform/index.js';"," import AxiosHeaders from '../core/AxiosHeaders.js';","+import cookies from '../helpers/cookies.js';"," import { progressEventReducer } from '../helpers/progressEventReducer.js';"," import resolveConfig from '../helpers/resolveConfig.js';"," import { toByteStringHeaderObject } from '../helpers/sanitizeHeaderValue.js';","@@ -16,15 +17,34 @@ const isXHRAdapterSupported = typeof XMLHttpRequest !== 'undefined';"," export default isXHRAdapterSupported &&","   function (config) {","     return new Promise(function dispatchXhrRequest(resolve, reject) {","-      const _config = resolveConfig(config);","+      let useAsyncXsrf;","+      try {","+        const store =","+          platform.hasStandardBrowserEnv && typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.cookieStore;","+        useAsyncXsrf = store && utils.isFunction(store.get);","+      } catch (e) {","+        // A restricted Cookie Store getter must retain the synchronous fallback.","+      }","+      let xsrfCookieName;","+      const _config = resolveConfig(","+        config,","+        useAsyncXsrf","+          ? (name) => {","+              xsrfCookieName = name;","+              return null;","+            }","+          : undefined","+      );","       let requestData = _config.data;","       const requestHeaders = AxiosHeaders.from(_config.headers).normalize();","       let { responseType, onUploadProgress, onDownloadProgress } = _config;","       let onCanceled;","+      let timeoutId;","       let uploadThrottled, downloadThrottled;","       let flushUpload, flushDownload, flushDownloadWithEvent;"," ","       function done() {","+        clearTimeout(timeoutId);","         flushUpload && flushUpload(); // flush events","         flushDownload && flushDownload(); // flush events"," ","@@ -177,6 +197,7 @@ export default isXHRAdapterSupported &&"," ","       // Handle timeout","       request.ontimeout = function handleTimeout() {","+        if (!request) return;","         let timeoutErrorMessage = _config.timeout","           ? 'timeout of ' + _config.timeout + 'ms exceeded'","           : 'timeout exceeded';","@@ -201,13 +222,6 @@ export default isXHRAdapterSupported &&","       // Remove Content-Type if data is undefined","       requestData === undefined && requestHeaders.setContentType(null);"," ","-      // Add headers to the request","-      if ('setRequestHeader' in request) {","-        utils.forEach(toByteStringHeaderObject(requestHeaders), function setRequestHeader(val, key) {","-          request.setRequestHeader(key, val);","-        });","-      }","-","       // Add withCredentials to request if needed","       if (!utils.isUndefined(_config.withCredentials)) {","         request.withCredentials = !!_config.withCredentials;","@@ -244,12 +258,14 @@ export default isXHRAdapterSupported &&","             return;","           }","           reject(!cancel || cancel.type ? new CanceledError(null, config, request) : cancel);","-          request.abort();","+          const xhr = request;","           done();","           request = null;","+          xhr.abort();","         };"," ","         _config.cancelToken && _config.cancelToken.subscribe(onCanceled);","+        if (!request) return;","         if (_config.signal) {","           _config.signal.aborted","             ? onCanceled()","@@ -257,6 +273,8 @@ export default isXHRAdapterSupported &&","         }","       }"," ","+      if (!request) return;","+","       const protocol = parseProtocol(_config.url);"," ","       if (protocol && !platform.protocols.includes(protocol)) {","@@ -271,7 +289,72 @@ export default isXHRAdapterSupported &&","         return;","       }"," ","-      // Send the request","-      request.send(requestData || null);","+      const sendRequest = () => {","+        if (!request) return;","+        // Apply headers after an asynchronous XSRF read so existing headers are","+        // replaced through AxiosHeaders rather than appended by the native XHR.","+        if ('setRequestHeader' in request) {","+          utils.forEach(","+            toByteStringHeaderObject(requestHeaders),","+            function setRequestHeader(val, key) {","+              request.setRequestHeader(key, val);","+            }","+          );","+        }","+        request.send(requestData || null);","+      };","+","+      if (xsrfCookieName) {","+        // Native XHR timeout starts at send(). Cover cookie preparation and the","+        // subsequent request with the same budget and existing timeout handler.","+        const now =","+          typeof performance !== 'undefined' && utils.isFunction(performance.now)","+            ? () => performance.now()","+            : Date.now;","+        const deadline = request.timeout > 0 ? now() + Number(request.timeout) : undefined;","+        const abortOnTimeout = () => {","+          if (!request) return;","+          const xhr = request;","+          xhr.ontimeout();","+          xhr.abort();","+        };","+        if (deadline !== undefined) {","+          const scheduleTimeout = () => {","+            const remaining = deadline - now();","+            if (remaining > 0) {","+              // Browser timers overflow above the signed 32-bit delay limit.","+              timeoutId = setTimeout(scheduleTimeout, Math.min(remaining, 0x7fffffff));","+            } else {","+              abortOnTimeout();","+            }","+          };","+          scheduleTimeout();","+        }","+","+        cookies","+          .readAsync(xsrfCookieName)","+          .then((value) => {","+            if (!request) return;","+            // Promise callbacks may run before an overdue timer after a busy task.","+            if (deadline !== undefined && now() >= deadline) {","+              abortOnTimeout();","+              return;","+            }","+            if (value) {","+              const headerName =","+                utils.hasOwnProp(_config, 'xsrfHeaderName') && _config.xsrfHeaderName;","+              requestHeaders.set(headerName, value);","+            }","+            sendRequest();","+          })","+          .catch((error) => {","+            if (!request) return;","+            reject(AxiosError.from(error, null, config, request));","+            done();","+            request = null;","+          });","+      } else {","+        sendRequest();","+      }","     });","   };"],"additions":94,"deletions":11,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/helpers/cookies.js","lines":["@@ -1,6 +1,14 @@"," import utils from '../utils.js';"," import platform from '../platform/index.js';"," ","+const decodeCookieValue = (value) => {","+  try {","+    return decodeURIComponent(value);","+  } catch (e) {","+    return value;","+  }","+};","+"," export default platform.hasStandardBrowserEnv","   ? // Standard browser envs support document.cookie","     {","@@ -30,26 +38,39 @@ export default platform.hasStandardBrowserEnv"," ","       read(name) {","         if (typeof document === 'undefined') return null;","+        const cookieString = document.cookie;","+        if (!cookieString) return null;","         // Match name=value by splitting on the semicolon separator instead of building a","         // RegExp from `name` — interpolating an unescaped string into a RegExp would let","         // metacharacters (e.g. `.+?` in an attacker-influenced cookie name) cause ReDoS or","         // match the wrong cookie. Browsers may serialize cookie pairs as either \";\" or","         // \"; \", so ignore optional whitespace before each cookie name.","-        const cookies = document.cookie.split(';');","+        const cookies = cookieString.split(';');","         for (let i = 0; i < cookies.length; i++) {","           const cookie = cookies[i].replace(/^\\s+/, '');","           const eq = cookie.indexOf('=');","           if (eq !== -1 && cookie.slice(0, eq) === name) {","-            try {","-              return decodeURIComponent(cookie.slice(eq + 1));","-            } catch (e) {","-              return cookie.slice(eq + 1);","-            }","+            return decodeCookieValue(cookie.slice(eq + 1));","           }","         }","         return null;","       },"," ","+      async readAsync(name) {","+        try {","+          const store = typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.cookieStore;","+          if (store && utils.isFunction(store.get)) {","+            const cookie = await store.get(name);","+            // Both APIs expose stored bytes; preserve Axios's existing URI decoding.","+            return cookie ? decodeCookieValue(cookie.value) : null;","+          }","+        } catch (e) {","+          // Restricted or unavailable storage retains the synchronous fallback.","+        }","+","+        return this.read(name);","+      },","+","       remove(name) {","         this.write(name, '', Date.now() - 86400000, '/');","       },","@@ -60,5 +81,8 @@ export default platform.hasStandardBrowserEnv","       read() {","         return null;","       },","+      async readAsync() {","+        return null;","+      },","       remove() {},","     };"],"additions":30,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/helpers/resolveConfig.js","lines":["@@ -22,7 +22,9 @@ const encodeUTF8 = (str) =>","     String.fromCharCode(parseInt(hex, 16))","   );"," ","-function resolveConfig(config) {","+const readCookie = (name) => cookies.read(name);","+","+function resolveConfig(config, readXsrfCookie = readCookie) {","   const newConfig = mergeConfig({}, config);"," ","   // Read only own properties to prevent prototype pollution gadgets","@@ -104,7 +106,7 @@ function resolveConfig(config) {","       withXSRFToken === true || (withXSRFToken == null && isURLSameOrigin(newConfig.url));"," ","     if (shouldSendXSRF) {","-      const xsrfValue = xsrfHeaderName && xsrfCookieName && cookies.read(xsrfCookieName);","+      const xsrfValue = xsrfHeaderName && xsrfCookieName && readXsrfCookie(xsrfCookieName);"," ","       if (xsrfValue) {","         headers.set(xsrfHeaderName, xsrfValue);"],"additions":4,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/browser/cookies.browser.test.js","lines":["@@ -62,6 +62,25 @@ describe('helpers::cookies (vitest browser)', () => {","     }","   });"," ","+  it('returns null when document.cookie is undefined', () => {","+    const descriptor = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(document, 'cookie');","+","+    Object.defineProperty(document, 'cookie', {","+      configurable: true,","+      get() {},","+    });","+","+    try {","+      expect(cookies.read('foo')).toBeNull();","+    } finally {","+      if (descriptor) {","+        Object.defineProperty(document, 'cookie', descriptor);","+      } else {","+        delete document.cookie;","+      }","+    }","+  });","+","   it('removes cookies', () => {","     cookies.write('foo', 'bar');","     cookies.remove('foo');"],"additions":19,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/browser/xsrf.browser.test.js","lines":["@@ -68,9 +68,10 @@ const clearXsrfCookie = () => {"," "," const sendRequest = async (url, config) => {","   const responsePromise = axios(url, config);","+","+  await vi.waitFor(() => expect(requests.at(-1)).toBeDefined());","   const request = requests.at(-1);"," ","-  expect(request).toBeDefined();","   await responsePromise;"," ","   return request;","@@ -81,12 +82,14 @@ describe('xsrf (vitest browser)', () => {","     requests = [];","     OriginalXMLHttpRequest = window.XMLHttpRequest;","     window.XMLHttpRequest = MockXMLHttpRequest;","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', undefined);","   });"," ","   afterEach(() => {","     clearXsrfCookie();","     window.XMLHttpRequest = OriginalXMLHttpRequest;","     vi.restoreAllMocks();","+    vi.unstubAllGlobals();","   });"," ","   it('should not set xsrf header if cookie is null', async () => {","@@ -103,6 +106,97 @@ describe('xsrf (vitest browser)', () => {","     expect(request.requestHeaders[axios.defaults.xsrfHeaderName]).toBe('12345');","   });"," ","+  it('should decode the xsrf value from cookieStore when available', async () => {","+    const get = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({","+      name: axios.defaults.xsrfCookieName,","+      value: 'raw%2Fvalue',","+    });","+    const readSpy = vi.spyOn(cookies, 'read');","+","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', { get });","+","+    const request = await sendRequest('/foo');","+","+    expect(get).toHaveBeenCalledWith(axios.defaults.xsrfCookieName);","+    expect(readSpy).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+    expect(request.requestHeaders[axios.defaults.xsrfHeaderName]).toBe('raw/value');","+  });","+","+  it('should fall back to document.cookie if cookieStore.get rejects', async () => {","+    setXsrfCookie('fallback');","+    const get = vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error('cookieStore unavailable'));","+    const readSpy = vi.spyOn(cookies, 'read');","+","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', { get });","+","+    const request = await sendRequest('/foo');","+","+    expect(get).toHaveBeenCalledWith(axios.defaults.xsrfCookieName);","+    expect(readSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith(axios.defaults.xsrfCookieName);","+    expect(request.requestHeaders[axios.defaults.xsrfHeaderName]).toBe('fallback');","+  });","+","+  it('should not read cookieStore for a cross-origin request by default', async () => {","+    const get = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ value: 'secret' });","+","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', { get });","+","+    const request = await sendRequest('http://example.com/');","+","+    expect(get).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+    expect(request.requestHeaders[axios.defaults.xsrfHeaderName]).toBeUndefined();","+  });","+","+  it('should clean up cancellation while cookieStore.get is pending', async () => {","+    const source = axios.CancelToken.source();","+    const unsubscribeSpy = vi.spyOn(source.token, 'unsubscribe');","+","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', {","+      get: vi.fn(() => new Promise(() => {})),","+    });","+","+    const responsePromise = axios('/foo', { cancelToken: source.token });","+","+    await vi.waitFor(() => expect(source.token._listeners).toHaveLength(1));","+    source.cancel('canceled');","+","+    await expect(responsePromise).rejects.toMatchObject({ code: 'ERR_CANCELED' });","+    expect(unsubscribeSpy).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();","+    expect(requests).toHaveLength(0);","+  });","+","+  it('should clean up an abort signal while cookieStore.get is pending', async () => {","+    const controller = new AbortController();","+    const removeEventListenerSpy = vi.spyOn(controller.signal, 'removeEventListener');","+","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', {","+      get: vi.fn(() => new Promise(() => {})),","+    });","+","+    const responsePromise = axios('/foo', { signal: controller.signal });","+","+    controller.abort();","+","+    await expect(responsePromise).rejects.toMatchObject({ code: 'ERR_CANCELED' });","+    expect(removeEventListenerSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith('abort', expect.any(Function));","+    expect(requests).toHaveLength(0);","+  });","+","+  it('should not read cookieStore or dispatch XHR for an already aborted signal', async () => {","+    const controller = new AbortController();","+    const get = vi.fn(() => new Promise(() => {}));","+","+    controller.abort();","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', { get });","+","+    await expect(axios('/foo', { signal: controller.signal })).rejects.toMatchObject({","+      code: 'ERR_CANCELED',","+    });","+","+    expect(get).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+    expect(requests).toHaveLength(0);","+  });","+","   it('should not set xsrf header if xsrfCookieName is null', async () => {","     setXsrfCookie('12345');"," "],"additions":95,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/browser/xsrfCookieStore.browser.test.js","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,359 @@","+import { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';","+import axios from '../../index.js';","+import cookies from '../../lib/helpers/cookies.js';","+import { nativeCookieStore } from '../setup/nativeCookieStore.js';","+","+const NativeXMLHttpRequest = window.XMLHttpRequest;","+","+let requests;","+let completeRequests;","+let controllers;","+","+class MockXMLHttpRequest {","+  constructor() {","+    this.requestHeaders = {};","+    this.status = 200;","+    this.statusText = 'OK';","+    this.responseText = '';","+    this.onloadend = null;","+    this.timeout = 0;","+  }","+","+  open() {}","+","+  setRequestHeader(name, value) {","+    this.requestHeaders[name] = this.requestHeaders[name]","+      ? this.requestHeaders[name] + ', ' + value","+      : value;","+  }","+","+  getAllResponseHeaders() {","+    return '';","+  }","+","+  send() {","+    requests.push(this);","+    if (completeRequests) queueMicrotask(() => this.onloadend());","+  }","+","+  abort() {","+    this.onabort && this.onabort();","+  }","+}","+","+const startRequest = (config = {}) => {","+  const controller = new AbortController();","+  controllers.push(controller);","+  const result = {};","+  result.promise = axios","+    .get('/cookie-store', {","+      adapter: 'xhr',","+      signal: controller.signal,","+      ...config,","+    })","+    .then(","+      (response) => {","+        result.response = response;","+      },","+      (error) => {","+        result.error = error;","+      }","+    );","+  return { result, controller };","+};","+","+describe('XHR Cookie Store compatibility', () => {","+  beforeEach(() => {","+    requests = [];","+    controllers = [];","+    completeRequests = true;","+    vi.stubGlobal('XMLHttpRequest', MockXMLHttpRequest);","+  });","+","+  afterEach(() => {","+    controllers.forEach((controller) => controller.abort());","+    document.cookie = 'XSRF-TOKEN=; max-age=0; path=/';","+    vi.useRealTimers();","+    vi.restoreAllMocks();","+    vi.unstubAllGlobals();","+  });","+","+  it.each([","+    ['abc%2Fdef%3D', 'abc/def='],","+    ['literal%252F', 'literal%2F'],","+    ['a+b', 'a+b'],","+    ['malformed%E0%A4%A', 'malformed%E0%A4%A'],","+    ['', undefined],","+  ])('preserves the existing header for cookie %s on every read path', async (stored, expected) => {","+    document.cookie = `XSRF-TOKEN=${stored}; path=/`;","+    for (const store of [","+      undefined,","+      { get: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ value: stored }) },","+      { get: vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error('unavailable')) },","+    ]) {","+      vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', store);","+      const response = await axios.get('/cookie-store', { adapter: 'xhr' });","+      expect(response.request.requestHeaders['X-XSRF-TOKEN']).toBe(expected);","+    }","+  });","+","+  it.runIf(nativeCookieStore).each(['abc%2Fdef%3D', 'literal%252F', 'a+b', 'malformed%'])(","+    'round-trips a real browser cookie through Cookie Store: %s',","+    async (stored) => {","+      document.cookie = `XSRF-TOKEN=${stored}; path=/`;","+      const expected = cookies.read('XSRF-TOKEN');","+      const readSpy = vi.spyOn(cookies, 'read');","+      vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', nativeCookieStore);","+","+      expect((await nativeCookieStore.get('XSRF-TOKEN')).value).toBe(stored);","+      const response = await axios.get('/cookie-store', { adapter: 'xhr' });","+","+      expect(response.request.requestHeaders['X-XSRF-TOKEN']).toBe(expected);","+      expect(readSpy).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+    }","+  );","+","+  it.each([{ xsrfCookieName: null }, { xsrfHeaderName: null }, { withXSRFToken: false }])(","+    'does not start a cookie read when XSRF is disabled: %j',","+    async (config) => {","+      const get = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ value: 'secret' });","+      const readSpy = vi.spyOn(cookies, 'readAsync');","+      vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', { get });","+      await axios.get('/cookie-store', { adapter: 'xhr', ...config });","+      expect(get).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+      expect(readSpy).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+    }","+  );","+","+  it('does not fall back to a stale cookie when Cookie Store returns no match', async () => {","+    document.cookie = 'XSRF-TOKEN=stale; path=/';","+    vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', { get: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(null) });","+    const readSpy = vi.spyOn(cookies, 'read');","+    const response = await axios.get('/cookie-store', { adapter: 'xhr' });","+    expect(response.request.requestHeaders['X-XSRF-TOKEN']).toBeUndefined();","+    expect(readSpy).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+  });","+","+  it.runIf(nativeCookieStore)(","+    'sends a decoded token through native Cookie Store and native XHR',","+    async () => {","+      document.cookie = 'XSRF-TOKEN=abc%2Fdef%3D; path=/';","+      vi.stubGlobal('cookieStore', nativeCookieStore);","+      vi.stubGlobal('XMLHttpRequest', NativeXMLHttpRequest);","+      const setHeader = vi.spyOn(NativeXMLHttpRequest.prototype, 'setRequestHeader');","+      const response = await axios.get(new URL('../../package.json', import.meta.url).href, {","+        adapter: 'xhr',","+        timeout: 5000,","+      });","+      expect(response.status).toBe(200);","+      expect(setHeader).toHaveBeenCalledWith('X-XSRF-TOKEN', 'abc/def=');","+    }","+  );","+","+  it('keeps Fetch on its existing synchronous cookie reader', async () => {","+    document.cookie = 'XSRF-T